          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "work-template-design"
        },
        "markdown": "## Questions for Codex\n\n1. Should `work` become a first-class `artifactKind`, or remain a graph template first?\n2. Which sections deserve dedicated node types versus ordinary authored content?\n3. Should every work expose a graph-owned entry port through its declaration?\n4. Which fields belong in the declaration, and which belong only in the visible experience?\n5. How should optional sections collapse without leaving layout holes?\n6. Should related works use explicit semantic edges, portals, or both?\n7. What is the smallest valid work that still feels complete?\n\n### Proposed minimum\n\n**Declaration + Hero + Summary + Primary Experience + Connections**\n\nEverything else is optional enrichment.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784508920038,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    }
